WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.525
Let’s pull the whole buoyage system into one table.

2
00:00:03.775 --> 00:00:08.650
If you know this table, you can name almost any mark the exam describes.

3
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.800
Starboard-side lateral marks: red, with a red light.

4
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.875
Port-side lateral marks: green, with a green light.

5
00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:25.400
Preferred channel marks: red and green bands, with a composite group-flashing light, two plus one, in the color of the top band.

6
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:31.575
Safe water marks: red and white vertical stripes, with a white light flashing Morse A.

7
00:00:31.825 --> 00:00:38.025
Isolated danger marks: black with red bands, and a white light flashing in groups of two.

8
00:00:38.275 --> 00:00:41.400
Special marks: yellow, with a yellow light.

9
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.625
Notice the pattern in the lights.

10
00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:48.400
Red and green lights are only on lateral marks.

11
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:52.450
White lights are on safe water and isolated danger.

12
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.550
Yellow is special.

13
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.675
That’s lesson four.

14
00:00:56.925 --> 00:00:59.175
Morse A means safe water.

15
00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:02.325
Two balls and two flashes mean danger.

16
00:01:02.575 --> 00:01:05.375
On the Intracoastal, follow the yellow.

17
00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:09.025
Next time: lights, and how far you can see them.
